        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.443,
            0.845,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "？ Analyse and interpret each of the observations you made. Share appropriate summary/conclusion statements."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.486,
            0.847,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": "In Punjab, the monthly maximum temperature increases from January to June, reaching a high of $3 8 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } ;$ Then, it reduces to just under $3 5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$ in July, stays mostly flat till September, and then falls continuously till December, reaching about $2 3 ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C } .$ January has the lowest among the monthly maximum temperature of about $1 9 ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.583,
            0.847,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "Kerala’s trend is different — it stays mostly flat throughout the year. The peak is around $3 3 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$ in April and the lowest point is around $2 9 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C }$ in July. Notice that the monthly maximum temperatures in"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.639,
            0.66,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "Kerala are similar both in summer and winter!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.662,
            0.656,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "In short, the temperature in Punjab varies more, reaching colder and warmer temperatures than in Kerala."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.722,
            0.712,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": "This can trigger questions in different directions, some of which can be answered using data. Here are some directions to think about —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.784,
            0.722,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": "Why are the trends so distinct in these two states? What factors determine a region’s temperature?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.674,
            0.641,
            0.912,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
